Since this is an old game (and I wailed on it in the old days)
I'll throw out the answer without doing a spoiler (also, I don't
know how...hehe).

First, you must have a ring of teleport control and a ring of
fire protection.  You should of found a wand of wishing on every
level of the labyrinth so you can easily wish for them.  Then
find a level teleporter (often found in small 1 space rooms) in
LVs 15-20 or so.  Walk onto teleporter, when it asks where you
want to go type 40, and this will put you in lowest level of
dungeon for that game.  Telep control allows you to specify the
level you want to go to.  And since level 40 is HELL, then
without ring of fire protection you'd fry.  HeHe.  Wizard is
on lowest level but you may want to work your way down to lv
27 to get wands and build xp.  (oops, I mean up to lv 27 then
go back to lv40, kill wizard (you'll need a ring of levit or
a potion of levit or a lot of rocks and a wand of digging or
a pickaxe) then (depending on whether you want to keep bulking
up on xp or not) find lv teleporter, teleport to lv1 and out.

I usually fought my way back up to bulk my final points (and
that wiz is a pesky little bugger).  Grin.


